      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.09,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "So you learned how to work with NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 5.7,
          "en": "or to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.7,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "you learned how to work with the NextJS App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "which is the most modern and recommended way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "of working with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "But if you take a look at the official documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "you might notice that there also is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "this Pages Router being mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "and in the documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "you can also switch between the App Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "and the Pages Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 33.09,
          "en": "And I also did mention the Pages Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.09,
          "end": 34.92,
          "en": "earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 39.92,
          "en": "Because indeed, NextJS offers two different approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.59,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "of building NextJS applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "You can use the so-called Pages Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "and the so-called App Router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 50.88,
          "en": "And you did learn about the App Router in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.88,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "but it's the Pages Router that has been around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "for a longer time period.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 59.94,
          "en": "It's the old way of building NextJS applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.94,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 62.7,
          "en": "though, that sounds as if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.7,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "it would be bad to use the Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.25,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "and that's absolutely not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 71.03999999999999,
          "en": "Instead, the Pages Router is very stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.03999999999999,
          "end": 73.77,
          "en": "because it's been around for many years,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.77,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "and it's being used in many existing NextJS projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "It allows you to build feature-rich full-stack apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 85.32,
          "en": "with React and NextJS just like the App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.32,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "and therefore, learning about the Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "even though it's not the recommended and most modern way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "of building NextJS applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "can still be a very good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "And you might need it for the job",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "you are going to work on in the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "if you are joining a team that's using the Pages Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 107.82,
          "en": "you need to know about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.82,
          "end": 109.62,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.62,
          "end": 111.36,
          "en": "you'll learn about the App Router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 114.87,
          "en": "which was introduced with NextJS 13,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.87,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "and which is marked as stable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 118.38,
          "en": "but which in my experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.38,
          "end": 121.59,
          "en": "still has some problems here and there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.59,
          "end": 123.81,
          "en": "maybe not in all apps you're using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.81,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "but it still can have some issues at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "But it does support, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 131.82,
          "en": "modern NextJS and React features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.82,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "like React Server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "and you can, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "build modern full-stack React apps with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 139.74,
          "en": "and it is the future of NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 139.74,
          "end": 143.46,
          "en": "that is why I covered it right from the start in-depth",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.46,
          "end": 144.81,
          "en": "in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.81,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "But the lectures and sections after this lecture here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 151.98,
          "en": "will now cover the Pages Router in-depth,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.98,
          "end": 156.09,
          "en": "because that was the original NextJS course I created,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.09,
          "end": 158.55,
          "en": "and I decided to keep it online",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 158.55,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "because learning about the Pages Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "and using the Pages Router is still a good idea,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "still something that makes sense for a lot of developers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "Now, if you don't care,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 172.89,
          "en": "you can, of course, ignore those lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
